From: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>
Subject: kABI workaround for missing v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor symbol
Patch-mainline: Never, kABI workaround
References: CVE-2026-68205 bsc#1274934

The patch
  patches.suse/media-v4l2-fwnode-Fix-subdev-owner-overwritten-in-v4.patch
changed the exported symbol v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor to
__v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor.

Provide the old function (but with a warning message) for kABI
compatibility, just calling the new function with NULL module.

Signed-off-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Petr Pavlu <petr.pavlu@suse.com>

---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-fwnode.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-fwnode.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-fwnode.c
@@ -1348,6 +1348,15 @@ out_cleanup:
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(__v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor);
 
+/* FIXME: for kABI workaround, provide the original version */
+#undef v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor
+int __must_check v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(struct v4l2_subdev *sd)
+{
+	pr_warn("Unfixed v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor is used\n");
+	return __v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(sd, NULL);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor);
+
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Sakari Ailus <sakari.ailus@linux.intel.com>");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Sylwester Nawrocki <s.nawrocki@samsung.com>");
